title: qt basics (pyside6)
url:   https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/
tags:  qt qt6 pyside pyside6 python gui start install import enum version

; Source of truth: PySide6 6.12.0 in /src/notes-goblin/qt/.venv (the .pyi stubs hold the exact signatures).

## docs and sources
doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6             # read the PySide6 docs: Python signatures, tutorials, examples  @docs @reference  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/>
doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/api.html    # list every PySide6 module with its classes  @modules @index  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/api.html>
doc.qt.io/qt-6                      # read the Qt 6 C++ docs; deeper text, same class and method names as Python  @cpp @docs  <https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/>
doc.qt.io/qt-6/classes.html         # list every Qt class A-Z  @all @index  <https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/classes.html>
.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/PySide6/QtWidgets.pyi  # read exact Python signatures of every widget method  @stubs @signature  <file:/src/notes-goblin/qt/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/PySide6/QtWidgets.pyi>
.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/PySide6/QtCore.pyi  # read exact signatures for QtCore (signals, timers, files, models)  @stubs  <file:/src/notes-goblin/qt/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/PySide6/QtCore.pyi>
.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/PySide6/QtGui.pyi  # read exact signatures for QtGui (painting, images, actions, text)  @stubs  <file:/src/notes-goblin/qt/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/PySide6/QtGui.pyi>
rg "def setText" .venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/PySide6/*.pyi  # find which classes have a method, with its signature  @grep @search
help(QWidget.setLayout)             # show a method signature in the Python REPL  @signature @repl
code.qt.io pyside-setup examples    # browse the official PySide6 example programs  @example @sample  <https://code.qt.io/cgit/pyside/pyside-setup.git/tree/examples?h=6.12>
doc.qt.io/qt-6/qtexamplesandtutorials.html  # browse all Qt examples and tutorials (C++, same ideas)  @example @tutorial  <https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qtexamplesandtutorials.html>

## install and version
uv add pyside6                      # add PySide6 (Essentials + Addons) to a uv project  @install @pip
pip install pyside6                 # install PySide6 with pip  @install
pip install pyside6-essentials      # install only the core modules (Core, Gui, Widgets, Network, Qml, Quick...)  @install @small
pip install pyside6-addons          # install the extra modules (Charts, Multimedia, WebEngine, 3D, Pdf...)  @install @extra
PySide6.__version__                 # get the PySide6 version string, e.g. "6.12.0"  @version
PySide6.__version_info__            # get the version as a tuple, e.g. (6, 12, 0, "", "")  @version @tuple
QtCore.qVersion()                   # get the version of the Qt C++ libraries at run time  @version  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/index.html>
QtCore.__version__                  # get the Qt version the PySide6 module was built with  @version
QLibraryInfo.version()              # get the Qt version as a QVersionNumber  @version  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QLibraryInfo.html#PySide6.QtCore.QLibraryInfo.version>
QLibraryInfo.path(QLibraryInfo.LibraryPath.PluginsPath)  # find where Qt plugins (platforms, styles, imageformats) live  @plugins  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QLibraryInfo.html#PySide6.QtCore.QLibraryInfo.path>
QLibraryInfo.isDebugBuild()         # check if Qt is a debug build  @debug  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QLibraryInfo.html#PySide6.QtCore.QLibraryInfo.isDebugBuild>
python -c "import PySide6, os; print(os.path.dirname(PySide6.__file__))"  # print the PySide6 install folder  @path @where

## imports
from PySide6.QtCore import Qt, QObject, Signal, Slot, QTimer  # import core: enums, signals, timers, models, files  @import  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/index.html>
from PySide6.QtGui import QColor, QFont, QIcon, QAction, QKeySequence  # import gui: colors, fonts, icons, actions, painting  @import  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/index.html>
from PySide6.QtWidgets import QApplication, QWidget, QVBoxLayout  # import widgets: everything you see in a desktop window  @import  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/index.html>
from PySide6 import QtCore, QtGui, QtWidgets  # import whole modules; then write QtWidgets.QLabel  @import @namespace
QAction                             # lives in QtGui in Qt 6 (QtWidgets in Qt 5)  @importerror @qt5  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QAction.html>
QShortcut                           # lives in QtGui in Qt 6 (QtWidgets in Qt 5)  @importerror @qt5  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QShortcut.html>
QUndoStack / QUndoCommand           # live in QtGui in Qt 6; QUndoView stays in QtWidgets  @importerror @qt5  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QUndoStack.html>
QFileSystemModel                    # import from QtWidgets in PySide6  @importerror  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QFileSystemModel.html>
QStandardItemModel / QStandardItem  # import from QtGui, not QtCore  @importerror  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QStandardItemModel.html>
QSvgWidget                          # import from QtSvgWidgets; QtSvg only has the renderer and generator  @importerror @svg  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtSvgWidgets/QSvgWidget.html>
QOpenGLWidget                       # import from QtOpenGLWidgets in Qt 6  @importerror @opengl  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtOpenGLWidgets/QOpenGLWidget.html>
QRegExp                             # gone in Qt 6; use QRegularExpression  @qt5 @removed  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QRegularExpression.html>
QDesktopWidget                      # gone in Qt 6; use QScreen (QGuiApplication.primaryScreen())  @qt5 @removed  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QScreen.html>

## application and event loop
app = QApplication(sys.argv)        # create the one app object before any widget  @start @main  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QApplication.html>
app = QApplication([])              # create the app without command line arguments  @start
sys.exit(app.exec())                # run the event loop until the last window closes, then exit with its code  @mainloop @run  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QApplication.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QApplication.exec>
    import sys
    from PySide6.QtWidgets import QApplication, QLabel
    app = QApplication(sys.argv)
    w = QLabel("Hello"); w.show()
    sys.exit(app.exec())
exec() vs exec_()                   # use exec(); exec_() is the old Qt 5 name, still there but deprecated  @qt5 @deprecated
QCoreApplication(sys.argv)          # create an app with no GUI (command line tools, servers)  @console @headless  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QCoreApplication.html>
QGuiApplication(sys.argv)           # create an app with a GUI but no widgets (QML / QWindow only)  @qml  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QGuiApplication.html>
QApplication.instance()             # get the running app object, or None  @existing @singleton  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QCoreApplication.html#PySide6.QtCore.QCoreApplication.instance>
QCoreApplication.instanceExists()   # check if an app object already exists  @existing  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QCoreApplication.html#PySide6.QtCore.QCoreApplication.instanceExists>
app.quit()                          # stop the event loop (exec() returns 0)  @exit @close  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QCoreApplication.html#PySide6.QtCore.QCoreApplication.quit>
app.exit(CODE)                      # stop the event loop and make exec() return CODE  @exit  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QCoreApplication.html#PySide6.QtCore.QCoreApplication.exit>
app.aboutToQuit.connect(FN)         # run cleanup just before the event loop ends  @shutdown @cleanup  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QCoreApplication.html#PySide6.QtCore.QCoreApplication.aboutToQuit>
app.setQuitOnLastWindowClosed(False)  # keep running after the last window closes (tray apps)  @tray  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QGuiApplication.html#PySide6.QtGui.QGuiApplication.setQuitOnLastWindowClosed>
app.lastWindowClosed.connect(FN)    # react when the last window was closed  @close  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QGuiApplication.html#PySide6.QtGui.QGuiApplication.lastWindowClosed>
QApplication.processEvents()        # let the UI repaint during a long loop (better: move the work to a thread)  @freeze @hang  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QCoreApplication.html#PySide6.QtCore.QCoreApplication.processEvents>
app.setApplicationName("NAME")      # set the app name (used by QSettings, QStandardPaths)  @name  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QCoreApplication.html#PySide6.QtCore.QCoreApplication.setApplicationName>
app.setOrganizationName("ORG")      # set the organization name (used by QSettings)  @settings  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QCoreApplication.html#PySide6.QtCore.QCoreApplication.setOrganizationName>
app.setOrganizationDomain("example.com")  # set the domain (used by QSettings on macOS)  @settings  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QCoreApplication.html#PySide6.QtCore.QCoreApplication.setOrganizationDomain>
app.setApplicationVersion("1.0")    # set the version shown by QCommandLineParser --version  @version  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QCoreApplication.html#PySide6.QtCore.QCoreApplication.setApplicationVersion>
app.setApplicationDisplayName("My App")  # set the name shown in window titles  @title  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QGuiApplication.html#PySide6.QtGui.QGuiApplication.setApplicationDisplayName>
app.setWindowIcon(QIcon("icon.png"))  # set the default icon for all windows  @icon  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QGuiApplication.html#PySide6.QtGui.QGuiApplication.setWindowIcon>
app.setDesktopFileName("org.example.app")  # link the app to its .desktop file (Wayland icon, taskbar)  @linux @wayland  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QGuiApplication.html#PySide6.QtGui.QGuiApplication.setDesktopFileName>
QCoreApplication.arguments()        # get the command line arguments as a list of str  @argv  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QCoreApplication.html#PySide6.QtCore.QCoreApplication.arguments>
QCoreApplication.applicationDirPath()  # get the folder of the running executable  @path  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QCoreApplication.html#PySide6.QtCore.QCoreApplication.applicationDirPath>
QCoreApplication.applicationPid()   # get the process id  @pid  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QCoreApplication.html#PySide6.QtCore.QCoreApplication.applicationPid>
QGuiApplication.platformName()      # get the platform plugin in use: "xcb", "wayland", "offscreen"...  @platform  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QGuiApplication.html#PySide6.QtGui.QGuiApplication.platformName>
QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen python app.py  # run without a display (CI, tests, screenshots)  @headless @ci
QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb python app.py   # force X11 instead of Wayland  @wayland @x11
QT_DEBUG_PLUGINS=1 python app.py    # print why a plugin (e.g. platform "xcb") fails to load  @plugin @error
QApplication.setStyle("Fusion")     # use the Fusion style, same look on every OS  @style @theme  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QApplication.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QApplication.setStyle>
QApplication.clipboard()            # get the system clipboard  @copy @paste  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QGuiApplication.html#PySide6.QtGui.QGuiApplication.clipboard>
QApplication.primaryScreen()        # get the main screen (size, dpi)  @monitor @display  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QGuiApplication.html#PySide6.QtGui.QGuiApplication.primaryScreen>
QApplication.screens()              # list all screens  @monitor  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QGuiApplication.html#PySide6.QtGui.QGuiApplication.screens>
QApplication.allWidgets()           # list every widget that exists  @debug  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QApplication.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QApplication.allWidgets>
QApplication.topLevelWidgets()      # list all windows  @windows  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QApplication.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QApplication.topLevelWidgets>
QApplication.activeWindow()         # get the window that has keyboard focus  @focus  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QApplication.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QApplication.activeWindow>
QApplication.focusWidget()          # get the widget that has keyboard focus  @focus  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QApplication.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QApplication.focusWidget>
QApplication.widgetAt(QCursor.pos())  # get the widget under the mouse  @hover  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QApplication.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QApplication.widgetAt>
app.focusChanged.connect(FN)        # react when focus moves: FN(old, new)  @focus  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QApplication.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QApplication.focusChanged>
QApplication.beep()                 # play the system bell  @sound  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QApplication.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QApplication.beep>
QApplication.alert(WINDOW)          # flash the taskbar entry of a window  @attention  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QApplication.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QApplication.alert>
QApplication.setOverrideCursor(Qt.CursorShape.WaitCursor)  # show a busy cursor everywhere  @busy @wait  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QGuiApplication.html#PySide6.QtGui.QGuiApplication.setOverrideCursor>
QApplication.restoreOverrideCursor()  # remove the busy cursor again  @busy  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QGuiApplication.html#PySide6.QtGui.QGuiApplication.restoreOverrideCursor>
with QOverrideCursorGuard(Qt.CursorShape.WaitCursor):  # show a busy cursor only inside the with-block (new in 6.12)  @busy @context  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QOverrideCursorGuard.html>
QApplication.keyboardModifiers()    # check which of Shift/Ctrl/Alt is held right now  @modifier  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QGuiApplication.html#PySide6.QtGui.QGuiApplication.keyboardModifiers>
QApplication.mouseButtons()         # check which mouse buttons are held right now  @mouse  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QGuiApplication.html#PySide6.QtGui.QGuiApplication.mouseButtons>
QGuiApplication.styleHints().colorScheme()  # check if the system uses dark or light mode  @dark @theme  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QStyleHints.html#PySide6.QtGui.QStyleHints.colorScheme>
QGuiApplication.styleHints().colorSchemeChanged.connect(FN)  # react when the system switches dark/light mode  @dark  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QStyleHints.html#PySide6.QtGui.QStyleHints.colorSchemeChanged>
QGuiApplication.styleHints().setColorScheme(Qt.ColorScheme.Dark)  # force dark (or Light) mode for this app  @dark @theme  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QStyleHints.html#PySide6.QtGui.QStyleHints.setColorScheme>
QGuiApplication.setHighDpiScaleFactorRoundingPolicy(Qt.HighDpiScaleFactorRoundingPolicy.PassThrough)  # keep fractional scaling (150%) as is; call before the app  @hidpi @scale  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtGui/QGuiApplication.html#PySide6.QtGui.QGuiApplication.setHighDpiScaleFactorRoundingPolicy>
QT_SCALE_FACTOR=1.5 python app.py   # scale the whole UI by a factor  @hidpi @zoom
QCoreApplication.setAttribute(Qt.ApplicationAttribute.AA_DontShowIconsInMenus)  # set an app-wide attribute; call before creating the app  @attribute  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QCoreApplication.html#PySide6.QtCore.QCoreApplication.setAttribute>

## objects and ownership
QObject(parent)                     # create an object owned by PARENT; it is deleted when the parent is deleted  @parent @memory  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QObject.html>
QWidget(parent)                     # create a child widget drawn inside PARENT; no parent means a new window  @parent @window  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QWidget.html>
self.win = MainWindow()             # keep a Python reference to a parentless window or it is garbage collected and vanishes  @gc @disappear
obj.deleteLater()                   # delete a QObject safely once control returns to the event loop  @delete @free  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QObject.html#PySide6.QtCore.QObject.deleteLater>
obj.setParent(NEW)                  # move an object to a new parent (owner)  @reparent  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QObject.html#PySide6.QtCore.QObject.setParent>
obj.parent()                        # get the owning object  @tree  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QObject.html#PySide6.QtCore.QObject.parent>
obj.children()                      # list direct children  @tree  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QObject.html#PySide6.QtCore.QObject.children>
obj.findChild(QPushButton, "okButton")  # find one child by type and objectName (searches all levels)  @find @lookup  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QObject.html#PySide6.QtCore.QObject.findChild>
obj.findChildren(QLineEdit)         # list all children of a type  @find  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QObject.html#PySide6.QtCore.QObject.findChildren>
obj.findChildren(QLineEdit, options=Qt.FindChildOption.FindDirectChildrenOnly)  # list only direct children of a type  @find  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QObject.html#PySide6.QtCore.QObject.findChildren>
obj.setObjectName("NAME")           # give an object a name for findChild, stylesheets (#NAME) and debugging  @id @name  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QObject.html#PySide6.QtCore.QObject.setObjectName>
obj.inherits("QAbstractButton")     # check the C++ class hierarchy by class name  @isinstance  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QObject.html#PySide6.QtCore.QObject.inherits>
obj.metaObject().className()        # get the class name, e.g. "QPushButton"  @type @class  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QMetaObject.html#PySide6.QtCore.QMetaObject.className>
obj.dumpObjectTree()                # print the child tree to the debug output  @debug  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QObject.html#PySide6.QtCore.QObject.dumpObjectTree>
obj.setProperty("NAME", VALUE)      # set a Qt property, or add a dynamic one (usable in stylesheets)  @dynamic  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QObject.html#PySide6.QtCore.QObject.setProperty>
obj.property("NAME")                # read a Qt property by name  @dynamic  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QObject.html#PySide6.QtCore.QObject.property>
obj.dynamicPropertyNames()          # list the names of dynamic properties  @dynamic  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QObject.html#PySide6.QtCore.QObject.dynamicPropertyNames>
obj.destroyed.connect(FN)           # run FN when the C++ object is deleted  @delete @signal  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QObject.html#PySide6.QtCore.QObject.destroyed>
obj.tr("Text")                      # mark a string as translatable  @i18n @translate  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QObject.html#PySide6.QtCore.QObject.tr>
shiboken6.isValid(obj)              # check if the C++ object behind a Python wrapper still exists  @deleted @crash
shiboken6.delete(obj)               # delete the C++ object right now  @delete
shiboken6.getCppPointer(obj)        # get the C++ address of a wrapped object  @pointer @address
RuntimeError: Internal C++ object (...) already deleted.  # you used a wrapper whose C++ object was deleted (its parent died)  @error @crash
doc.qt.io/qt-6/objecttrees.html     # read how parents own and delete their children  @ownership @guide  <https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/objecttrees.html>

## enums and flags
Qt.AlignmentFlag.AlignCenter        # write enums with the full scope: Qt.EnumName.Value  @enum  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.AlignmentFlag>
Qt.AlignmentFlag.AlignRight | Qt.AlignmentFlag.AlignVCenter  # combine flags with |  @or @flags  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.AlignmentFlag>
FLAGS & Qt.KeyboardModifier.ShiftModifier  # test if one flag is set in a flag value  @and @test  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.KeyboardModifier>
Qt.AlignCenter                      # short old-style name; still works but not in the stubs, so the IDE complains  @enum @qt5
QMessageBox.StandardButton.Ok       # enums inside a class: Class.EnumName.Value  @enum @nested  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QMessageBox.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QMessageBox.StandardButton>
Qt.Key.Key_Escape.value             # get the integer behind an enum (Python enum.Enum)  @int @value  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.Key>
Qt.ItemDataRole(256)                # turn an int back into an enum value  @int @cast  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.ItemDataRole>
Qt.GlobalColor.red                  # use a predefined color  @color  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.GlobalColor>
Qt.Orientation.Horizontal / Qt.Orientation.Vertical  # pick a direction for sliders, splitters, headers  @orientation  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.Orientation>
Qt.CheckState.Checked / Unchecked / PartiallyChecked  # set or read a check box state  @checkbox  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.CheckState>
Qt.SortOrder.AscendingOrder / DescendingOrder  # set the sort direction  @sort  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.SortOrder>
Qt.CaseSensitivity.CaseInsensitive  # ignore case in filters and searches  @case  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.CaseSensitivity>
Qt.MatchFlag.MatchContains          # find items whose text contains the search text  @find  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.MatchFlag>
Qt.TextFormat.RichText / PlainText / MarkdownText / AutoText  # tell a label how to read its text  @html @markdown  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.TextFormat>
Qt.CursorShape.PointingHandCursor   # use a hand mouse cursor (also WaitCursor, IBeamCursor, CrossCursor...)  @cursor  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.CursorShape>
Qt.MouseButton.LeftButton / RightButton / MiddleButton  # name a mouse button  @mouse  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.MouseButton>
Qt.KeyboardModifier.ControlModifier  # name the Ctrl key (Cmd on macOS); also ShiftModifier, AltModifier, MetaModifier  @ctrl @modifier  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.KeyboardModifier>
Qt.Key.Key_Return / Key_Enter / Key_Escape / Key_Delete  # name keys in key events  @keyboard  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.Key>
Qt.DayOfWeek.Monday                 # name a weekday  @date  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.DayOfWeek>
Qt.DateFormat.ISODate               # format dates as ISO 8601  @date @iso  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.DateFormat>
Qt.TimerType.PreciseTimer           # ask for ms-accurate timers (default CoarseTimer is ~5%)  @timer  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.TimerType>
Qt.ConnectionType.QueuedConnection  # deliver a signal later through the event loop  @signal @thread  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/Qt.html#PySide6.QtCore.Qt.ConnectionType>
@QEnum                              # register a Python enum.Enum in the meta-object system (for QML and properties)  @enum @decorator  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/index.html>
    from enum import Enum
    class Car(QObject):
        @QEnum
        class Brand(Enum):
            Volvo, Saab = range(2)
@QFlag                              # register a Python enum.Flag in the meta-object system  @flag @decorator  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/index.html>

## __feature__ (snake_case, true_property)
from __feature__ import snake_case  # call Qt methods in snake_case: w.set_window_title(...)  @pep8 @feature
from __feature__ import true_property  # use properties as attributes: w.windowTitle = "x" instead of setWindowTitle  @property @feature
from __feature__ import snake_case, true_property  # turn on both features; affects only this module  @feature
    from PySide6.QtWidgets import QApplication, QLabel
    from __feature__ import snake_case, true_property
    app = QApplication([])
    w = QLabel("hi")
    w.window_title = "Demo"   # was: w.setWindowTitle("Demo")
    w.show(); app.exec()
; The feature switch only renames things for the module that imports it; other modules keep camelCase.

## logging and debug output
qDebug("text")                      # print a debug message through Qt's message handler  @log @print  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/index.html>
qInfo("text") / qWarning("text") / qCritical("text")  # print a message with a level  @log @warn @error  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/index.html>
qFatal("text")                      # print and abort the program  @log @abort  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/index.html>
qInstallMessageHandler(FN)          # catch all Qt messages: FN(mode, context, message)  @log @handler  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/index.html>
    def handler(mode, ctx, msg):
        print(f"{mode.name} {ctx.file}:{ctx.line} {msg}")
    qInstallMessageHandler(handler)
qSetMessagePattern("%{type} %{file}:%{line} %{message}")  # change the format of Qt log lines  @log @format  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/index.html>
QT_MESSAGE_PATTERN="[%{time}] %{message}" python app.py  # change the log format from the environment  @log @env
QT_LOGGING_RULES="qt.*.debug=true" python app.py  # turn on Qt's internal debug categories  @log @verbose
QLoggingCategory.setFilterRules("qt.network.ssl=true")  # turn logging categories on or off in code  @log @category  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QLoggingCategory.html#PySide6.QtCore.QLoggingCategory.setFilterRules>
QLoggingCategory("my.app")          # create your own logging category  @log @category  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QLoggingCategory.html>
qCDebug(CATEGORY, b"text")          # print a debug message in a category (message is bytes)  @log  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/index.html>
QtMsgType.QtWarningMsg              # name the message levels: QtDebugMsg, QtInfoMsg, QtWarningMsg, QtCriticalMsg, QtFatalMsg  @log @level  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QtMsgType.html>
python -X faulthandler app.py       # print the Python stack when Qt crashes with a segfault  @crash @segfault

## translation (i18n)
self.tr("Hello")                    # mark a string in a QObject subclass for translation  @i18n @translate  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QObject.html#PySide6.QtCore.QObject.tr>
QCoreApplication.translate("CONTEXT", "Hello")  # translate outside a QObject  @i18n  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QCoreApplication.html#PySide6.QtCore.QCoreApplication.translate>
QT_TR_NOOP("Hello")                 # mark a string for lupdate without translating it now  @i18n  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/index.html>
translator = QTranslator(); translator.load("app_de.qm")  # load a compiled translation file  @i18n @qm  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QTranslator.html#PySide6.QtCore.QTranslator.load>
translator.load(QLocale(), "app", "_", ":/i18n")  # load app_<lang>.qm for the user's locale from resources  @i18n @locale  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QTranslator.html#PySide6.QtCore.QTranslator.load>
app.installTranslator(translator)   # turn on a loaded translation  @i18n  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QCoreApplication.html#PySide6.QtCore.QCoreApplication.installTranslator>
QLibraryInfo.path(QLibraryInfo.LibraryPath.TranslationsPath)  # find Qt's own translations (qtbase_de.qm)  @i18n  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QLibraryInfo.html#PySide6.QtCore.QLibraryInfo.path>
changeEvent(e) with e.type() == QEvent.Type.LanguageChange  # retranslate the UI when the language changes at run time  @i18n @retranslate  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtCore/QEvent.html#PySide6.QtCore.QEvent.Type>

## common errors
ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'PySide6'  # wrong Python: activate the venv or use uv run  @install @venv
qt.qpa.plugin: Could not load the Qt platform plugin "xcb"  # install libxcb-cursor0 (Debian/Ubuntu) or use QT_QPA_PLATFORM=wayland  @linux @x11
QWidget: Must construct a QApplication before a QWidget  # create QApplication first, at the top of main  @order @crash
QObject::startTimer: Timers can only be used with threads started with QThread  # touch timers/objects only in their own thread  @thread
QObject: Cannot create children for a parent that is in a different thread  # create the object in the worker thread, or moveToThread()  @thread
window opens and closes at once     # you kept no reference to it; store it on self or a variable that lives on  @gc @disappear
UI freezes                          # long work runs in the GUI thread; use QThread, QThreadPool or QTimer  @hang @freeze
TypeError: ... called with wrong argument types  # look at the overloads in the .pyi stub; PySide6 is strict about types  @signature @overload
